WEBVTT

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:20.170
© BF-WATCH TV 2021

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:11.620
Ro Weta

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:58.290
Valeria. - You put her on the earring.

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:04.020
- I've lost my mind. - Don't worry, you won't get away with it.

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:05.890
I'll teach you a lesson in water.

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:16.270
Get down, I'll jump on your back.

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:26.280
Hurry up, you wretch.

00:07:57.360 --> 00:07:58.710
Ma'am, the actors have arrived.

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:03.450
The missionaries should come. - When?

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:09.280
Today or tomorrow. One of them will stay at our place.

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:15.430
I hope you won't play with the child's earring.

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:22.240
I'm not a child anymore. He'll be here tonight.

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:34.800
At the age of 13, as your mother.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:44.080
I warn you, get rid of those earplugs.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:49.620
Your mother put them away on the day she went to the monastery.

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:55.000
Your father was a bishop. As you know, they're both in heaven.

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:58.610
Is there any secret in those earplugs?

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:06.620
No, I got it at the auction of this house from a certain constable.

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:29.700
You knew him? - Oh, my God!

00:09:31.400 --> 00:10:00.000
But it's a wedding, the bride is getting married.

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:44.790
It must be him. He died a long time ago.

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:47.490
Whom are you talking about, Granny?

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:54.260
You, and a few more steps.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.340
Yes, Granny.

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:01.800
Oh, hey.

00:12:31.880 --> 00:12:39.960
and once again returned to your hands.

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:45.110
My uncle Stabl strives to strengthen these earrings.

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:48.620
He has lost my father and mother,

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:50.680
and I am afraid of your fate.

00:12:50.680 --> 00:12:52.680
Today in the church,

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:58.550
today in the church, there will be a sermon for the Lord.

00:13:00.220 --> 00:13:06.020
Put your jackets on so I can say a few words to you during the ceremony.

00:13:07.350 --> 00:13:09.540
Your unhappy eagle.

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:30.000
-Valerie! -It's time to get dressed.

00:13:32.970 --> 00:13:35.990
I'll take the rosemary with me.

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:37.810
I came among you, gentlemen, to offer you a lesson.

00:15:37.810 --> 00:15:46.510
Oh, sir, you know what you are, you alabaster of Daniel.

00:15:46.510 --> 00:15:51.740
You are an unsheathed, granite apple.

00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:57.430
You are a little ship, opening its arms.

00:16:00.030 --> 00:16:18.500
But instead of the guardian angel, I will bow to you.

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:36.870
Amen.

00:17:33.520 --> 00:17:34.070
Rico.

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:06.720
He really made me sick.

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:11.240
Valeria, I want to tell you something.

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:15.290
We're in the city. - I'm sorry.

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:26.020
Don't look. I'm already here. For the first time.

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:06.180
♪

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:35.120
Where is the poor man, my dear child?

00:19:37.080 --> 00:19:38.710
Sir!

00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:47.640
Will you do me a favour or do you not like me?

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:57.680
No, sir, I don't like you.

00:20:25.720 --> 00:20:26.980
I'm hungry

00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:09.530
They are close.

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:30.000
You don't like me anymore, my dear Graziana.

00:21:30.320 --> 00:21:33.120
When will you think about it?

00:21:33.120 --> 00:21:35.640
I don't know.

00:22:16.280 --> 00:22:17.250
Me and the star.

00:22:31.080 --> 00:22:43.350
I could love him when I love him. - That's why.

00:22:43.430 --> 00:22:59.570
Where are you going, constable? Hands up, you thief!

00:23:00.090 --> 00:23:00.960
Or I'll shoot!

00:23:01.690 --> 00:23:05.920
Elsa, it's me.

00:23:06.820 --> 00:23:09.930
You didn't recognize me?

00:23:12.620 --> 00:23:15.780
Richard!

00:23:16.850 --> 00:23:21.150
How long has it been since someone called me that?

00:23:25.720 --> 00:23:29.030
Why did you come, Richard?

00:23:30.730 --> 00:23:31.990
I miss her again.

00:23:35.070 --> 00:23:40.040
Since you took me away and left me,

00:23:40.510 --> 00:23:44.110
I've never loved any man.

00:23:45.260 --> 00:23:57.910
Oh, my dear, you were 17 at the time.

00:23:58.010 --> 00:24:00.000
What would I give for it if I could have a child?

00:24:00.060 --> 00:24:04.590
Richard, give me back your secrets.

00:24:04.670 --> 00:24:07.780
I'll give you everything you want.

00:24:07.860 --> 00:24:18.120
Give me back this house, Elso.

00:24:18.200 --> 00:24:23.230
That means stealing Valeria.

00:24:23.310 --> 00:24:28.990
You're determined to commit far worse crimes.

00:24:36.400 --> 00:24:38.270
I will listen to all of you.

00:24:38.270 --> 00:24:40.270
All right.

00:24:40.270 --> 00:24:45.940
We are signing a small purchase agreement.

00:24:45.940 --> 00:24:49.690
You will be young and beautiful again.

00:24:49.690 --> 00:24:54.840
This is what will happen tonight at the wedding of my godfather.

00:24:54.840 --> 00:24:56.920
You are a devil.

00:25:00.280 --> 00:25:02.600
The devil will save you.

00:25:02.600 --> 00:25:04.600
Where is Valeria?

00:25:04.600 --> 00:25:05.750
I took her with me.

00:25:05.750 --> 00:25:07.870
Where?

00:25:07.870 --> 00:25:10.470
To the tower of the church.

00:25:10.470 --> 00:25:12.670
Bring her to me, you fool.

00:25:12.670 --> 00:25:14.390
You will bring me there.

00:26:21.180 --> 00:26:22.150
I don't know.

00:26:34.800 --> 00:26:46.140
You hear? The bells rang for the third time and then they went silent again.

00:26:52.550 --> 00:27:00.000
You know, after many troubles,

00:27:00.190 --> 00:27:06.010
I've experienced terrible things when I was in their place.

00:27:08.210 --> 00:27:12.840
We saved a young blackbird. She was very beautiful.

00:27:12.870 --> 00:27:15.120
What happened to her, my dear sir?

00:27:17.440 --> 00:27:23.300
We took her to our barn and turned her into our faith.

00:27:25.790 --> 00:27:30.000
- She proved to be very talented. - Is she really a bird?

00:27:31.790 --> 00:27:37.040
Unfortunately, we lost her in a French attack.

00:27:37.120 --> 00:27:39.860
Marta, where is the wine?

00:27:39.940 --> 00:27:43.500
I'll tell you what happened to her.

00:27:43.580 --> 00:27:45.580
She fell into terrible danger

00:27:45.660 --> 00:27:51.100
and committed a sin against the Sixth Commandment.

00:27:51.180 --> 00:27:54.260
I'll give you a lesson in that regard, my dear child.

00:27:54.340 --> 00:27:57.130
Thank you, Your Honor.

00:27:57.210 --> 00:28:00.000
Your father, Bishop, was a gentle man.

00:28:02.750 --> 00:28:09.010
and adorned him with the most beautiful women.

00:28:09.290 --> 00:28:10.760
I'll tell you about it sometime.

00:28:12.760 --> 00:28:14.590
How many children did he have?

00:28:14.800 --> 00:28:19.490
You and a boy named Orlik.

00:28:20.720 --> 00:28:23.970
- Orlik? - What?

00:28:26.310 --> 00:28:29.090
My head aches, I can't sleep.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:33.540
It's not over yet. - I'm sorry.

00:28:34.330 --> 00:28:39.930
Will you drink with us? - I've never drunk wine.

00:28:40.280 --> 00:28:50.390
You'll make a drink for yourself. - In memory of the deceased bishop.

00:29:00.410 --> 00:29:01.190
Orlík!

00:29:47.660 --> 00:29:50.320
I'd like to talk to you, my dear child.

00:29:50.860 --> 00:29:52.470
Now, my honourable sir?

00:29:53.050 --> 00:29:55.210
This is not the best time to get distracted.

00:29:55.350 --> 00:29:58.200
Where is my child?

00:30:00.830 --> 00:30:08.480
What I want from you is sweet.

00:30:42.990 --> 00:30:44.630
What have you done?

00:31:44.560 --> 00:31:57.720
Perfect. The house is yours again.

00:32:01.690 --> 00:32:09.090
And now we'll wait for the holy hour.

00:33:02.140 --> 00:33:13.990
It's a pity for my hopes.

00:33:32.270 --> 00:33:33.110
You can be.

00:34:09.850 --> 00:34:11.780
- Do you love me? - I do.

00:34:36.650 --> 00:34:45.430
Your blood is so coarse, you look so old.

00:35:10.750 --> 00:35:11.400
I don't want to read it.

00:35:42.540 --> 00:35:52.820
Please, don't look at me like that.

00:36:04.350 --> 00:36:05.540
- Don't you feel cold? - No.

00:36:13.800 --> 00:36:21.320
A wonderful room for guests. You'll have a good rest.

00:36:22.480 --> 00:36:25.760
A poor man came to me from the tower.

00:36:26.280 --> 00:36:27.940
He saved my heart from the bell.

00:36:30.320 --> 00:36:35.640
I heard a strange ringing. I prayed for you.

00:36:41.250 --> 00:36:47.340
The sea is our best friend.

00:36:48.470 --> 00:36:51.410
If my uncle Constable doesn't have enough fresh blood,

00:36:51.840 --> 00:36:53.960
- he'll be like an animal. - You're so cruel!

00:36:54.570 --> 00:36:56.400
He's been ripe for death for a hundred years.

00:37:08.250 --> 00:37:10.760
It's nothing. It's just a hanging man.

00:37:18.410 --> 00:37:26.600
Where are we? - Under your house.

00:37:28.110 --> 00:37:29.220
I'm afraid.

00:37:32.810 --> 00:37:37.230
- Who's in those watermelons? - The victims of the bloodshed.

00:37:37.410 --> 00:37:38.100
Take a look.

00:38:20.380 --> 00:38:27.460
Sorry, I wasn't dressed properly. This is your room.

00:38:33.160 --> 00:38:35.220
I thought the room was empty.

00:38:36.480 --> 00:38:38.420
I came by night.

00:38:39.840 --> 00:38:44.180
Don't you know me? I'm your distant sister.

00:38:44.860 --> 00:38:46.160
Call me Elza.

00:38:47.490 --> 00:38:53.400
Valérie. And this is my brother.

00:38:54.460 --> 00:39:00.000
Orlik. - I sat in your room.

00:39:01.180 --> 00:39:04.140
- As I see it. - I think so.

00:39:05.250 --> 00:39:07.960
No, no, give me another one.

00:39:09.420 --> 00:39:14.880
- I'll talk to the granny. - Your granny has left, my dear child.

00:39:16.380 --> 00:39:20.770
- Without saying goodbye? - Old people have different ways of saying goodbye.

00:39:22.260 --> 00:39:30.000
- I'm sure you'll allow me to live in her room. - With pleasure.

00:39:32.200 --> 00:39:39.830
So the room is yours? - Yes, please.

00:39:44.570 --> 00:39:58.900
I'd like to ride my horse right away. - I'll lend you mine.

00:40:02.080 --> 00:40:04.100
I'm very tired. I'm going to bed.

00:40:09.100 --> 00:40:13.020
You don't know me, do you, Valeria?

00:40:13.030 --> 00:40:25.180
I hope you're not afraid of me.

00:40:27.980 --> 00:40:30.000
You're so dear to me.

00:40:32.270 --> 00:40:33.810
We always see each other for the first time.

00:42:25.240 --> 00:42:25.830
My headphones!

00:43:00.250 --> 00:43:02.600
Hasn't your sister come back yet?

00:43:03.570 --> 00:43:05.320
Where is Valeria? You know that.

00:43:07.200 --> 00:43:09.800
You're so sweet when you're angry.

00:43:10.460 --> 00:43:11.620
Where is Valeria?

00:43:15.590 --> 00:43:17.790
I'll tell you under one condition.

00:43:19.160 --> 00:43:28.130
- You won't love me. - Never!

00:43:32.780 --> 00:43:37.650
Are you leaving? - No, I'm not your guest.

00:43:37.730 --> 00:43:41.520
You're leaving. - You'll regret it.

00:45:02.650 --> 00:45:15.200
until you saved Valeria.

00:45:16.080 --> 00:45:19.830
I heard that my sister-in-law loves you.

00:45:21.160 --> 00:45:27.330
She took my earrings.

00:45:31.820 --> 00:46:00.000
You mustn't. We're brothers and sisters.

00:46:00.410 --> 00:46:02.330
-But... -Your father was a demon too!

00:46:02.410 --> 00:46:05.550
That's not true! Come back, Valérie!

00:46:06.140 --> 00:46:11.840
Valérie, my father is a devil!

00:48:01.440 --> 00:48:03.440
She sacrificed herself for her youth.

00:48:07.170 --> 00:48:10.500
You are lost just like me.

00:48:13.370 --> 00:48:14.370
You will fall into the same pit.

00:48:16.250 --> 00:48:19.250
Only your granddaughter could save us both.

00:48:20.230 --> 00:48:21.550
She has my blood.

00:48:24.250 --> 00:48:26.710
What? Her father was a bishop after all.

00:48:27.660 --> 00:48:30.000
I am a bishop!

00:48:30.380 --> 00:48:34.060
It's me, Valeria.

00:48:34.410 --> 00:48:38.710
- You're alive. - Drink, drink.

00:48:38.790 --> 00:48:43.260
No, let's see how I prolong my youth.

00:48:43.560 --> 00:48:51.190
Save Valeria. Her blood is our salvation.

00:48:52.770 --> 00:48:57.750
Valeria, my beautiful Valeria.

00:49:16.640 --> 00:49:17.410
Take it.

00:50:08.280 --> 00:50:15.740
- You saved me. - Thank you.

00:50:20.030 --> 00:50:21.570
You bastard!

00:51:53.740 --> 00:51:55.380
Your darling.

00:52:04.540 --> 00:52:11.940
- Poor Gracia! - I've got a plan, Elsa.

00:52:12.000 --> 00:52:19.560
- I need Orlík's heart. - You want to kill Orlík?

00:52:19.800 --> 00:52:22.880
His heart will revive my daughter and give her eternal youth.

00:52:23.410 --> 00:52:27.300
Richard, bring Orlík's heart to my breasts.

00:52:27.420 --> 00:52:29.220
You're deceiving Valeria.

00:52:32.200 --> 00:52:35.160
Richard, you'll do it.

00:52:37.810 --> 00:52:42.000
With a bleeding heart.

00:53:16.280 --> 00:53:20.640
Help! Help! Why do you appear to me as Valeria?

00:53:21.120 --> 00:53:25.190
Don't worry, I'm not dead. And you're not either.

00:53:26.430 --> 00:53:28.550
Come on, I'll take you away from here.

00:53:36.040 --> 00:53:53.780
The woman is over there, sir. - Sinner! She made me sin! You'll see. - Valeria!

00:54:00.350 --> 00:54:05.170
You've forsaken me and the devil has disrespected your words.

00:54:05.250 --> 00:54:08.740
We could be happy together, but it's too late.

00:54:08.820 --> 00:54:15.050
Believe me, Valeria, the devil is neither your father nor mine.

00:54:15.130 --> 00:54:18.510
You've extended his life.

00:54:18.590 --> 00:54:21.430
I wanted to be your protector, friend and companion.

00:54:21.510 --> 00:54:27.020
It's too late. Goodbye, Valeria, your eagle.

00:54:27.100 --> 00:54:29.700
Valeria, what's the matter with you?

00:54:30.320 --> 00:54:55.670
- Come on. - Hedviga! - Daddy!

00:55:02.780 --> 00:55:24.230
I am in the power of a dragon, I have it on my shoulder.

00:55:32.460 --> 00:55:34.980
No. - Are you watching anything I do?

00:55:35.510 --> 00:55:37.670
No, why? - I have nothing to do with it.

00:55:39.570 --> 00:55:41.170
You ate fruit, didn't you?

00:55:49.160 --> 00:55:51.730
When you're with me, I'm not afraid of anything.

00:55:53.960 --> 00:55:57.810
I'm so happy. I've never had a girlfriend.

00:56:29.150 --> 00:56:30.000
Valéry, I'm sorry.

00:56:30.980 --> 00:56:35.030
Look, Hedviga, Skvrna is gone.

00:56:35.410 --> 00:56:43.690
Your kisses have brought me back my health.

00:56:43.890 --> 00:56:45.090
You're so beautiful.

00:56:46.560 --> 00:56:51.120
The witch is living among you.

00:56:51.440 --> 00:56:55.120
She cursed me with her sinful words.

00:56:55.740 --> 00:56:59.120
She looked at me from the side of the street.

00:57:00.410 --> 00:57:04.050
When she found out that I could resist her,

00:57:04.280 --> 00:57:06.320
she threw a rag at my neck.

00:57:07.970 --> 00:57:11.720
Thank God I was carried out alive and sound.

00:57:14.280 --> 00:57:18.770
But that witch is hiding among you!

00:57:20.060 --> 00:57:23.380
In the name of God, take her out! She belongs on the border!

00:57:23.540 --> 00:57:25.640
It's a lie! Don't believe him!

00:57:27.150 --> 00:57:29.700
That's her! The witch!

00:57:30.160 --> 00:57:32.520
Believe him, I promise you he's lying.

00:57:32.790 --> 00:57:35.450
And then there's Satan.

00:57:35.750 --> 00:57:37.910
Kill her! On the border with her!

00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:02.880
You witch!

00:58:02.880 --> 00:58:05.350
You're burning!

00:58:05.350 --> 00:58:13.050
You're making me sick!

00:58:13.050 --> 00:58:14.530
You filthy comedian!

01:01:03.840 --> 01:01:05.840
Come here, you sons of bitches!

01:01:05.840 --> 01:01:12.100
Do you want to live somewhere?

01:01:31.080 --> 01:01:58.550
You are deep, Richard.

01:03:50.640 --> 01:03:52.630
If only she'd stopped being a whore.

01:05:15.770 --> 01:05:26.530
Granny, are you back? - I'm back from church, dear child.

01:05:35.630 --> 01:05:54.540
The missionaries are gone. - What about your child? - Nothing.

01:06:15.480 --> 01:06:18.370
Granny, some unknown man?

01:06:22.420 --> 01:06:25.800
It's just one of the actors who's in town now.

01:06:54.800 --> 01:06:55.800
to the theatre.

01:07:01.280 --> 01:07:18.820
...and leave for the Blue Hill. - Shoot for God!

01:07:34.380 --> 01:07:42.910
Miss! Miss! Granny's dying!

01:07:42.910 --> 01:07:52.720
Granny! My dear granny, what's wrong?

01:08:01.980 --> 01:08:28.800
- A heart-throb! - A cat without a cat! - That's a good sign.

01:08:30.990 --> 01:08:37.740
I've never had the courage to tell you the truth.

01:08:41.880 --> 01:08:45.240
Your mother loved a certain thinker young man.

01:08:47.500 --> 01:08:56.290
She gave birth to two children, a boy and a girl.

01:08:58.250 --> 01:09:00.000
Oh, my God!

01:09:00.060 --> 01:09:04.190
Richard, my beloved, told me that the children were his.

01:09:04.670 --> 01:09:06.560
And I, out of jealousy,

01:09:06.840 --> 01:09:09.030
I kicked your mother out of the house.

01:09:10.230 --> 01:09:12.590
I left the girl alone.

01:09:13.450 --> 01:09:14.790
It was you.

01:09:15.540 --> 01:09:17.960
Richard took the girl from me, I don't know where.

01:09:19.080 --> 01:09:21.510
I kicked your mother out of the house.

01:09:21.950 --> 01:09:27.140
I'll take you in, only if the horses bring you.

01:09:27.460 --> 01:09:29.000
So my mother is alive?

01:10:08.570 --> 01:10:23.910
- Mom! - My child, this is your father, my dear.

01:10:30.000 --> 01:10:32.900
Father, I've known her for a long time.

01:10:32.900 --> 01:10:50.680
You remember her from your childhood, don't you?

01:10:50.680 --> 01:11:00.000
It's all just a dream.

01:11:00.060 --> 01:11:01.440
from your granny.
